Available Lead Magnet Formats
A lead magnet = content accessible only after filling out a form.
Choose the most relevant format based on the target audience and the brief. Justify your choice in a single sentence.
E-book / Whitepaper: dense content 10-30 pages, positions expertise. Ideal for B2B targets who need to be educated before buying. Avoid if the target wants a quick answer.
Checklist: a list of actions or verifications. Ideal when the target has a specific task to accomplish and wants a practical tool. Avoid if the subject is too complex to fit in a list.
X-Step Guide: sequential process with clear progression. Ideal for "how-to" topics. Avoid if steps vary too much depending on the context.
Quiz / Self-Assessment: interactive, personalizes the result based on responses. Ideal for engaging and qualifying at the same time. Avoid if the target is in a hurry or not digitally savvy.
Infographic: visualization of a concept, data, or process. Ideal for social media and data-driven topics. Avoid if the content is too nuanced to fit in a visual format.
Webinar / Replay: live or recorded session. Ideal for demonstrating deep expertise and building a human connection. Avoid if the target does not have 30-60 minutes to invest.
Case Study / Benchmark: concrete results from a client or sector. Ideal for targets in the decision phase who want social proof. Avoid at the top of the funnel if the target does not recognize the problem yet.

